.TH Objectspace-SHELL 1 "@DATE@" "Objectspace @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
osd-shell \- the Objectspace desktop and folder windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B osd-shell
.RB [ \-\-desktop
.RI [ FOLDER ]]
.RB [ \-\-details ]
.RI [ FOLDER ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B osd-shell
draws Objectspace's desktop and its windows: folder windows in icon, tree and
details views, settings notebooks, the Launcher, TheBar (in the
Objectspace session), Find, the Window List and Messages. Objects come from
.BR osdd ;
.B osd-shell
is one process per desktop.
.PP
With folders named, it opens a window on each. With none and without
.BR \-\-desktop ,
it shows the desktop as an ordinary full-screen window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-desktop " [" \fIFOLDER\fR ]
Be the desktop, on FOLDER (default: the XDG desktop folder). The Objectspace
session and the GNOME Shell extension start it so.
.TP
.B \-\-details
Open the named folders in details view.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OSD_THEBAR
1 shows TheBar, 0 hides it (default: shown in the Objectspace session).
.TP
.B OSD_NO_LAUNCHER
Do not show the Launcher at start.
.TP
.B OSD_NO_RESTORE
Do not reopen the windows open at the last logout.
.TP
.B OSD_NO_SOUND
No sounds for actions.
.TP
.B OSD_TERMINAL
The terminal for text-mode programs, as a command line (for example
.BR "ptyxis \-\-" ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR osdctl (1),
.BR osd-session (1)
